                <pb facs="0201" n="189" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg189"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20210/1126: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-03-22T19:00:00-03:00">March 22, 1942—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 23—12:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>992. Department’s 725, March 21, 9 p.m. When we give the police some of the
                    evidence we have they will probably know how we got it.</p>
                <p>If we do not give them any evidence they will not be disposed to hold the spies
                    because they have no evidence against them other than the captured radio
                    transmitter; they did not capture them operating it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
